% SVG images and embedded documents (design 3.16).
%   redocx build examples/media/media.rdx
% Word 2016 and later show chart.svg itself; older versions show the fallback picture
% (a grey placeholder unless fallback= names one). Word merges chapter.docx into the
% body when it opens the file; the table of contents lists its headings after updating.
% It converts note.rtf the same way; \include-rtf reads the same file into the document itself.

\document[lang=en-GB]

\toc

= Introduction

Flow by hour, as a vector graphic:

\image[alt="Bar chart of traffic flow by hour", width=60%]{chart.svg}

\embed-docx{chapter.docx}

\embed-rtf{note.rtf}

The same note, read by redocx:

\include-rtf{note.rtf}

= Conclusion

The embedded chapter keeps its lists and headings.
